  "problem": "The volume of a cone is decreasing at a rate of $0.8\\pi \\,{\\text{m}}^{3}\\text{/s}.$ The diameter of the cone is always one-half of its height.  Find the rate of the cone's radius decrease when the radius is $2\\,\\text{m}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n*Hint*: Assume that the rate of decrease is positive.\n\nThe radius is decreasing at a rate of\n{{field-1}} $\\text{ m/s}.$",
